图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Vibe code as a team. Plan, build, review and release with your AI assistant.","id":"gh:1267786584","install_available":false,"language":"Python","name":"papi","slug":"getpapi/papi","topics":["ai-agents","ai-coding","claude","claude-code","codex","cursor","dsh-plugin","mcp","mcp-server","model-context-protocol","project-management","vibe-coding","vs-code","windsurf"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Vibe code as a team. Plan, build, review and release with your AI assistant."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# PAPI"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**End-to-end project management for AI builders.**"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Your AI starts every session from zero. Your project stays on course."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"AI coding tools are great at writing code and terrible at holding a direction. Scope grows, plans ch"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"ange, and the decisions behind them get made in a chat window and lost there. PAPI keeps the project"},{"id":"p5s3","text":" on course. It gives your assistant structured plan, build, review and release cycles, plus a decisi"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"on trail recording what was chosen, what was dropped, and why. Your assistant writes and reads it wh"},{"id":"p5s5","text":"ile it works, so it stays current without anyone maintaining it."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"You connect it once. From then on, your assistant starts every session knowing which cycle you're on"},{"id":"p6s2","text":", what's in flight, and what to do next."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"If PAPI is useful, star the repo. It's how other people building with AI assistants find it."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"**Free to start.** The whole plan → build → review → release loop, on up to three projects, no card."},{"id":"p8s2","text":" Free runs a real project start to finish; it isn't a trial. Pricing."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"> **What this repo is.** Documentation, install guides, plugin and extension manifests, the PAPI age"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"nt skills, and the issue tracker. PAPI's engine is closed source and hosted — you connect to it, you"},{"id":"p9s3","text":" don't build it from here. The `@papi-ai/server` package on npm is the supported local runtime. The "},{"id":"p9s4","text":"contents of this repo are MIT."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"**Let your AI install it.** Paste this to your assistant — Cursor, Claude Code, Windsurf, Codex, VS "},{"id":"p11s2","text":"Code, or any other MCP client:"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"> Read https://getpapi.ai/llms.txt and set up PAPI"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Your assistant reads the runbook and walks you through the whole first run: checking it's in the rig"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"ht project folder, connecting, setting up your project, planning your first cycle, and building your"},{"id":"p13s3","text":" first task. It works in coding tools and in chat apps like claude.ai and ChatGPT, and you don't nee"},{"id":"p13s4","text":"d to be a developer. (The same runbook lives in this repo as llms.txt and llms-install.md if your as"},{"id":"p13s5","text":"sistant can't fetch URLs.)"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"**The one thing only you can do.** You need a free account at getpapi.ai. After that there are two w"},{"id":"p14s2","text":" only you can do.** You need a free account at getpapi.ai. After that there are two ways to connect:"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"- **Connection token (default).** Open the Connect panel on getpapi.ai, copy the project id and conn"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"ection token under \"This is your project\", and hand them to your assistant. It puts them in your too"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"l's config and PAPI works straight away, with no browser step.\n- **Browser sign-in.** Your assistant"},{"id":"p15s4","text":" adds the server and you approve it in the browser. No assistant can click through that screen for y"},{"id":"p15s5","text":"ou, and until you do the server shows `Needs authentication`."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Most tools only load a new connection when a conversation starts, so open a fresh conversation after"},{"id":"p16s2","text":" connecting and ask your assistant to run `orient`."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"### Prefer to wire it up yourself?"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"In Claude Code, the shortest path is the plugin — two lines, nothing to copy or edit:"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"The plugin carries the server config and the PAPI skills for each phase of the cycle: planning, buil"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"ding, reviewing and releasing. It also includes `check-mcp`, which diagnoses a connection that isn't"},{"id":"p20s3","text":" working, and `papi-verify`, which health-checks the current cycle."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Every tool also takes the same streamable-HTTP endpoint directly, `https://mcp.getpapi.ai/mcp`. In C"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"kes the same streamable-HTTP endpoint directly, `https://mcp.getpapi.ai/mcp`. In Claude Code that's:"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"Either way, finish with `/mcp` → **papi** → **Authenticate**. Or skip the browser step entirely with"},{"id":"p23s2","text":" the connection token from the Connect panel:"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"The DeepSeek Harness bundle is in this repo but is not yet published to npm, so the command below wo"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"n't resolve until it is. After creating a PAPI connection token, it will install with:"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"See PAPI for DeepSeek Harness for token handling, verification, compatibility, and removal."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"Per-tool config for Cursor, VS Code, Windsurf, Codex, and any generic MCP client is in docs/install."},{"id":"p28s2","text":"-tool config for Cursor, VS Code, Windsurf, Codex, and any generic MCP client is in docs/install.md."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"## What you get"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"- **plan** breaks your goals into a cycle of right-sized tasks, each with a build handoff your assis"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"tant can execute directly.\n- **build** tracks what was built, what surprised you, and what was disco"},{"id":"p30s3","text":"vered along the way.\n- **review and release** close the loop, so every cycle feeds the next plan.\n- "},{"id":"p30s4","text":"**strategy reviews** every few cycles step back and check direction, not just velocity.\n- **A dashbo"},{"id":"p30s5","text":"ard** at getpapi.ai shows your cycles, board, and decisions, so you can see the state of the project"},{"id":"p30s6","text":".ai shows your cycles, board, and decisions, so you can see the state of the project without asking."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"The methodology is the product: a plan, build, review, release loop your assistant runs with you, wh"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"ere each cycle's learnings feed the next plan. PAPI has been built with PAPI for every cycle in the "},{"id":"p31s3","text":"le's learnings feed the next plan. PAPI has been built with PAPI for every cycle in the badge above."},{"id":"p32s1","text":"*The hub opens on one question — what happens next. The cycle's progress through plan, build, review"},{"id":"p32s2","text":" and release sits under it.*"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"*The board is the full picture. Your assistant writes to it as a side effect of working, so it is cu"},{"id":"p33s2","text":"rrent without anyone maintaining it.*"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"## How PAPI differs from a tracker"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"Linear, Jira, Asana and Notion are built for people to write tickets and other people to read them. "},{"id":"p35s2","text":"They suit that job well, and plenty of teams keep using them."},{"id":"p36s1","text":"PAPI's board is written and read by your assistant as it works. Starting a build opens the task, fin"},{"id":"p36s2","text":"ishing it files the report, and releasing closes the cycle. You approve the plan and sign off the re"},{"id":"p36s3","text":"g it files the report, and releasing closes the cycle. You approve the plan and sign off the review."},{"id":"p37s1","text":"Taskmaster is a good way to break work into tasks inside a repo. PAPI adds state that lives outside "},{"id":"p37s2","text":"the repo and persists across tools: cycles, build reports, review verdicts, and Active Decisions who"},{"id":"p37s3","text":"se confidence changes as evidence arrives. The same project is available from Claude Code, Cursor, V"},{"id":"p37s4","text":"S Code, Codex and the others, so switching tools doesn't reset it. Moving from Taskmaster? See PAPI "},{"id":"p37s5","text":"and the others, so switching tools doesn't reset it. Moving from Taskmaster? See PAPI vs Taskmaster."},{"id":"p38s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
